  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "1) Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 + transformer (config_006, acc 0.653) is the current best, and multiprofile + scvi_n200 is clearly the strongest RNA pipeline. However, image-only (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), leaving open the critical question of whether image features add complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. 2) Question tested: Does concatenating resnet50 image features to the best RNA multiprofile transformer model (config_006) improve validation accuracy, or does the weak image signal dilute the RNA representation? This isolates the effect of adding the image modality as a single conceptual change (image + fusion) on top of the best known RNA baseline. 3) Why best use of budget: The answer determines the entire direction of the remaining search—pursuing multimodal configs (032-051) or focusing on RNA-only refinements. Without this result, spending experiments on more complex multimodal variants risks wasting budget on a modality that may not contribute. It is the highest-information experiment available because it directly tests the core multimodal hypothesis with minimal confounds."
}

